right to the interface.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:45.320
So here I have a boundary
between two material, 1 and 2.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:52.520
And say the one side, I
have distribution function.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:59.690
So f1 equals f0, 1 minus
tau 1 vx1 df0, 1/dx.

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:07.460
So this is on the first side.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.890
On second side, you
can write the same--

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:15.500
f2 equal f0,2 tau vx2 df0, 2/dx.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:20.300
So we're assuming that
it's valid to the boundary.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.830
Of course, this is
an approximation.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:23.390
I don't have a
good justification.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:29.300
In fact, it's only
you can say OK,

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:30.890
maybe in the case
of [? Lucien ?]

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:33.620
number is not very large.

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:35.630
Then you can say
most of the region

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.790
