00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:40.490
But turns out this
will actually work out

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:42.520
pretty wide range of
[? Lucien ?] number

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:44.900
in many cases.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:50.750
And then I'm going
to do the heat flux.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:54.320
So if I do heat flux, I can
do particle flux, any flux.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.610
But let me write the heat flux.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:58.580
So the heat flux--

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.670
and if I think about
the inside diffusion,

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:05.990
just think about the physics,
this is an inside domain.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.710
We say this is a deviation.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:11.300
So what it means the transport
is in the same material.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:14.600
What diffusion really
mean, the distribution

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:17.660
function f0 is isotropic,
so it's a sphere.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:25.220
And then say I have
a small deviation.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.160
And if my heat flow
is in this direction,

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:32.140
so I have in the forward,
I have a surplus.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:34.920
I work backward because
the velocity is a negative

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.180
because I have a deficiency.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:43.240
It's really, we emphasize is
this region that's the surplus.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:47.840
And this deficiency,
this two parts that

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:49.700
