and that could transmit.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:38.940
I'll have to multiply by the
transmittance from 1 to 2.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:46.950
So I say OK, I do my typical
polarization kx, ky, kz.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:52.990
This is a side one, so
everything I put into side one.

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:56.750
That's gain, I'm summing
my quantum states.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:13:01.200
And the vx1, so this is a vx1.

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:06.570
Vx1 must be positive.

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:08.650
That's the going
from left to right.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:12.350
So that means my kx1,
and that's the v vector,

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:13.595
must be larger than 0.

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.290
The wave is going
from left to right.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:25.960
And h-bar omega, and I have f1.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:37.070
And I have then say, tau 1 to 2,
the transmittance from 1 to 2.

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:39.440
For example, in
